• UseHttpLogging() Middleware:
o Function: Injects middleware into the pipeline to capture and log HTTP request and
response specifics.
o Strategic Placement: Incorporate this middleware early in your Program.cs to
comprehensively capture all incoming requests and their corresponding responses.
• HttpLoggingOptions:
o Customization Power: A gateway to fine-tuning your HTTP logging experience.
o Key Options:
▪ LoggingFields: Precisely control which data points are logged (e.g., request
path, method, status code, headers).
▪ RequestHeaders, ResponseHeaders: Dictate which specific headers are
included in the logs.
